cff-version: 0.0.0
message: "If you use this work, you MUST cite the speakers whose languages the corpus holds."
title: anchor_sift
abstract: >-
  A method that measures how far an object sits from the most disordered arrangement
  of its own parts. The reference is built by maximizing entropy under constraints the
  object itself supplies, so there is no training, no prior and no model of the domain.
  One construction, unchanged, has read a published crystal cell edge to 0.0006
  angstroms, an image width, a Vigenere key length, and a published dialect border
  inside Lushootseed that it was never shown. It knows nothing and it generates
  nothing. The Salishan corpus it is measured against is the speech of named people,
  hand extracted and verified in two directions against the papers it came from.
